  "notes": "Course codes, titles, and credit hours are verbatim from the official Elementary Education, B.S. requirements in the Oakland University 2024-2025 Undergraduate Catalog, Volume 3 (School of Education and Human Services). Minimum 120 credits; minimum 45 credits at Oakland University; minimum 32 credits at the 3000 level or above.\nThe catalog publishes requirements as a list (general education, preprofessional, professional), not a semester-by-semester schedule. Semester placement here follows the catalog's structure: preprofessional courses first (major standing, requiring EED 2000 with B or better, is required before the professional sequence), then the professional sequence, with EED 4950 Internship in the final semester per catalog requirement. Documented as an adviser-style sequencing, not a catalog-printed schedule.\nGlobal Perspective: the catalog recommends 'GEO 2000 Global Human Systems'; the course carrying that title in the 2024-2025 catalog is AN 2130 - Global Human Systems (4), which is recorded here.\nKnowledge Application: recorded as WRT 3062 Writing Center Studies and Tutoring Practice (4), one of the catalog's recommended options (also satisfies Writing Intensive in General Education). EED 3100 satisfies the Writing Intensive in the Major and U.S. Diversity requirements.\nCREDIT TOTAL: the specified requirements (preprofessional 20 + professional 48 + internship 12 + recommended general education 36, with MTE 2111 double-counted as Formal Reasoning) sum to 116 credits. A 4-credit elective placeholder is included to reach the catalog's 120-credit minimum.\nEED 4950 Internship in Elementary Education is listed as 9 to 12 credits and must be taken in the final semester; recorded at 12 credits with a choice note. Application is due one full academic year in advance; minimum grade of C required for graduation, B for certification recommendation.",
